{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-pm-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.48 part E: `rates-pm`, the Rates-scale twin of `process-pm-exhaust` -- running-exhaust PM10 and PM2.5 totals, organic and elemental carbon, sulfate, NonECPM and aerosol water -- for the gasoline-selected passenger car in Washtenaw County on road types 1 and 4, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. SulfatePMCalculator per speed bin: the four-species share matrix on each bin's own rate, PM2.5 summed from it and PM10 chained off PM2.5, at every bin of road types 2 to 5 and for off-network idle on road type 1. SulfatePMCalculator.sql carries emissionRate through each step beside emissionQuant, so the per-bin rate is the inventory's construction over the rate.\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `n_ratesScale` = 1 and `n_outputRate`, the (pollutant-process, road type, cohort) pairs across five road types, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "rates-pm"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
